WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:07.880
[Brett]: Oh, shit!

00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:09.020
Sorry Wren.

00:00:09.020 --> 00:00:10.600
[Nick]: Dude that's the first hambone right there.

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:11.960
[Wren]: DUDE! 1 DOLLAR!

00:00:12.220 --> 00:00:13.220
[Brett]: 1 dollar?!

00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:14.580
Dude I don't have a dollar.

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:15.820
I don't have a dollar today.

00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:17.800
[Wren]: Not wearing a helmet, this guy..

00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:19.800
[Ben]: Is everyone wearing new Christmas clothes?

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:21.800
*random noises of affirmation*

00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:25.780
[Ben]: My new Christmas shirt, my new Christmas pants, my new Christmas shoes..

00:00:25.780 --> 00:00:27.780
Why didn't you get any new Christmas clothes?

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:30.060
[Wren]: You can do that??

00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:30.720
[Ben]: Yeah.

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:32.720
[Nick]: Did you guys all see Rogue One?

00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:36.000
[Sam]: When you watch Rogue One, how do you feel?

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:38.840
[Wren]: Honestly, I was a little disappointed because everyone dies.

00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:41.320
I was kind of hoping they'd do something a little bit more interesting than that.

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:45.300
I walked out of it going: "That was a very pretty film! Those VFX were awesome!"

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:49.180
[Sam]: And that's kind of where it ends because there's nothing that really sticks with you

00:00:49.180 --> 00:00:51.520
[Niko]: You can't just be all negative Nancy's around here

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:53.520
How would you make a better Star Wars?

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:55.400
These big budget movies, they try to

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:58.640
to be perfect in every single way. They draw from a language of other

00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:02.160
movies. What you get is this basically this giant big,

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:08.760
recycled version of a film that kind of touches upon all the tiny little things, things you've already seen and felt before.

00:01:08.830 --> 00:01:14.039
It checks all your boxes for what a story needs, but it doesn't give you the same takeaway.

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:19.799
[Niko]: Here's the thing about Rogue One: main character Jyn, I can't name a single hard decision she makes in the entire film.

00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:24.119
She's a main character that loses her agency. It's considered bad writing to have a character, a

00:01:24.119 --> 00:01:26.309
main character, that is passive. What that means

00:01:26.309 --> 00:01:31.420
is that the character sits there and everybody else tells that character what to do. Everybody else pushes that character through the plot. Everybody else

00:01:31.420 --> 00:01:34.320
pushes that character through the story and the character says "Wooaah", along for the ride.

00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:36.660
Versus a character having to make hard, active decisions.

00:01:37.340 --> 00:01:42.140
Jyn didn't have a goal. She literally just sat there, and everybody else told her what to do. The best example of this is

00:01:42.140 --> 00:01:44.300
at the very end when they're getting those hard drives.

00:01:44.420 --> 00:01:45.220
Jyn

00:01:45.220 --> 00:01:47.940
stands by the side, while freaking

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:52.600
Cassian or whatever his name is, is the man operating the hard drive machine.

00:01:52.600 --> 00:01:54.900
Why isn't Jyn doing it? She was the main character.

00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:57.800
[Sam]: This weak character, kind of, on a roller coaster throughout the whole thing,

00:01:58.160 --> 00:01:59.500
that's a huuuuge

00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:00.480
byproduct

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:02.320
of the fact that these movies are

00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:07.680
constructed completely independent of the characters. When you plan these movies out to a tee where you know these

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:09.740
scenes are going to happen, blah blah blah, it's like the characters

00:02:09.750 --> 00:02:11.700
don't even matter anymore, you're just writing the plot.

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:14.700
You're forcing these characters to just ride along with these decisions you've made.

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:16.280
It's not interesting.

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:18.540
[Niko]: You want to know why the part with Darth Vader, at the end, killing guys,

00:02:18.540 --> 00:02:23.400
was so thrilling? It's not because you get to see Darth Vader kill guys. Seeing Darth Vader want something and

00:02:23.460 --> 00:02:29.060
ACTIVELY go and try and take it, and suddenly all his power comes out like and you're like "Holy shit this guy's a huge badass. I didn't know

00:02:29.060 --> 00:02:34.880
he was so scary. Cause the character's being active. He's going and he's making hard decisions. He's killing people to get his goals.

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:39.200
[Sam]: He has intentions, and he has obstacles. I love that thing. Thanks Aaron Sorkin.

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:41.200
[Niko]: Well what'd you think of Rogue One, Ben?

00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:47.580
[Ben]: Every movie has to like feed into the next movie nowadays and all the characters have to be around for all the sequels and I

00:02:47.580 --> 00:02:49.049
was just so happy that this movie

00:02:49.049 --> 00:02:49.799
was like "*bleep* it. We're just-

00:02:49.799 --> 00:02:53.609
everyone's dead. They didn't care and they weren't trying to just like set it up for a sequel.

00:02:53.609 --> 00:02:55.280
They were just like "This is what we're gonna do."

00:02:55.280 --> 00:02:56.100
[Niko]: Ben,

00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:58.100
there's six more movies that came after this one.

00:02:58.100 --> 00:03:01.500
[All]: *laughing*

00:03:02.020 --> 00:03:04.140
[Sam]: What's terrible about it is that you kind

00:03:04.140 --> 00:03:08.880
of go like... From the outset, the assumption is these characters aren't going to be that memorable because....

00:03:09.180 --> 00:03:11.920
This is it. This is all you got them for so it's like

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:16.080
you don't get to build characters that are like "Damn, like, I'm gonna cosplay as

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:17.680
this one character.

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:20.400
[Niko]: That said, there's a couple things that Rogue One did correctly.

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:22.120
One: there were no Jedi in the movie.

00:03:22.120 --> 00:03:23.980
Second thing that they did really well:

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:28.840
Acknowledging what most people said is a giant plot hole in Star Wars, which is "Why can you blow up a Death Star with the

00:03:28.860 --> 00:03:31.280
simple Proton Torpedo in a exhaust shaft.

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:34.080
Making it a character-based crisis of conscience

00:03:34.360 --> 00:03:37.180
is such a good way to approach that and is so compelling.

00:03:37.180 --> 00:03:38.440
[Wren]: And this is also all just,

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:43.520
completely ignoring the fact that it is a very beautiful film. The effects are like some of the best out there on the market

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:46.289
right now. It's like, yeah, but that's come to be expected from,

00:03:46.289 --> 00:03:47.040
you know,

00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:49.100
ILM and Disney Films, it's like, it's

00:03:49.110 --> 00:03:50.110
also just like

00:03:50.110 --> 00:03:51.800
beautifully polished just like, alright.

00:03:51.800 --> 00:03:53.320
[Niko]: In the trailer, there's a shot where

00:03:53.320 --> 00:03:56.640
Jyn is running to I think it's like the little platforms to like recenter the

00:03:56.640 --> 00:03:59.580
satellite dish, and a Tie Fighter rises up and cuts her off.

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:03.390
That shot was actually added by the trailer house. They were like "The shot's cool,

00:04:03.390 --> 00:04:06.960
we need to jazz it up" and they added the Tie Fighter themselves. Probably with Element 3D.

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:08.470
[Niko and Wren]: *laughing*

00:04:08.470 --> 00:04:13.109
[Niko]: So in a nutshell: if you want to make a better Star Wars movie, let your characters be active.

00:04:13.140 --> 00:04:15.480
Don't make them passive. Don't worry about plot

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:19.080
holes, like studios are so concerned with people picking apart the movies on Reddit. That's fine,

00:04:19.080 --> 00:04:20.709
they can do that. Just make a character

00:04:20.709 --> 00:04:25.559
that has drive and emotion and ambition, and the audience will be along for the ride. I mean that's why

00:04:25.560 --> 00:04:32.160
Luke Skywalker and Han Solo and Princess Leia are so compelling. Even in a sci-fi universe, all this crazy world building, make them character-based.

